{
  "file": "common childhood",
  "page": 91,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        69.04139709472656,
        57.98431396484375,
        390.0213623046875,
        84.36231231689453
      ],
      "text": "11. Evidence for Recommendations",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 22.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.2333984375,
        79.98431396484375,
        370.3114013671875,
        106.36231231689453
      ],
      "text": "for Treatment of Hypoglycaemia",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 22.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        190.5670166015625,
        389.2339782714844,
        203.75601196289062
      ],
      "text": "11.1\t Sublingual administration of sugar in treatment of hypoglycaemia",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        207.19261169433594,
        399.122802734375,
        220.6826171875
      ],
      "text": "Sublingual sugar may be used as an immediate first aid measure in managing",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        220.19261169433594,
        399.1029052734375,
        233.6826171875
      ],
      "text": "hypoglycaemia in children in situations where intravenous administration of glucose",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        233.19261169433594,
        177.34292602539062,
        246.6826171875
      ],
      "text": "may be impossible or delayed.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        248.5972900390625,
        252.91282653808594,
        262.5173034667969
      ],
      "text": "(Strong recommendation, low quality evidence)",
      "font": "MinionPro-BoldIt",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        264.86187744140625,
        399.12286376953125,
        278.3518981933594
      ],
      "text": "This recommendation places value on ease of use, low cost, and high availability in",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        277.86187744140625,
        341.1329040527344,
        291.3518981933594
      ],
      "text": "the absence of any serious risk, although the evidence is of low quality.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        302.3805236816406,
        231.48292541503906,
        314.3705139160156
      ],
      "text": "11.1.1\t Evidence and summary of findings",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Bold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        318.0351867675781,
        399.0629577636719,
        331.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "The panel identified two randomized controlled trials (RCTs) from Burkina Faso and",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        331.0351867675781,
        392.65277099609375,
        344.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "Mali, cited in a recent review of the management of hypoglycaemia [Achoki, 2010].",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        344.0351867675781,
        399.12152099609375,
        357.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "Barennes et al (2005) conducted an open-label, quazi-randomized trial of",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        357.0351867675781,
        399.0927429199219,
        370.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "intravenous glucose, sublingual sugar, and oral sugar in Burkina Faso. Children aged",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        370.0351867675781,
        399.15277099609375,
        383.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "6 months to 15 years presenting to the outpatient department were eligible if: 1) they",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        383.0351867675781,
        399.12274169921875,
        396.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "had symptoms and signs of either acute respiratory infection (excluding pneumonia)",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        396.0351867675781,
        399.0828857421875,
        409.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "or malaria; 2) the caregiver agreed to attend an appointment the next morning; and",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        409.0351867675781,
        291.4729309082031,
        422.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "3) they had a blood glucose level between 3.3 to 5 mmol/l.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        422.0351867675781,
        399.0713195800781,
        435.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "The study screened 156 children; 87 were excluded, including 19 children initially",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        435.0351867675781,
        399.0428161621094,
        448.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "assigned to the sublingual group, who swallowed the sugar within the first 10",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        448.0351867675781,
        399.1127624511719,
        461.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "minutes. Sixty-nine were randomized to one of five groups: 1) half a tablespoon of",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        461.0351867675781,
        399.04278564453125,
        474.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "water (n = 11); 2) IV glucose (8 mL of 30% dextrose administered in a single bolus);",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        474.0351867675781,
        399.0826721191406,
        487.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "3) oral glucose (2.5 g sugar); 4) single dose sublingual group (2.5 g of wet sugar under",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        487.0351867675781,
        399.0628967285156,
        500.52520751953125
      ],
      "text": "the tongue); or 5) double dose sublingual group. The main outcome was treatment",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        500.0351867675781,
        399.00286865234375,
        513.5252075195312
      ],
      "text": "failure: the proportion of children who did not reach blood glucose >5.6 during the",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        513.03515625,
        112.39288330078125,
        526.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "study period.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        526.03515625,
        399.13140869140625,
        539.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "Baseline characteristics were similar across groups. There were no treatment",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        539.03515625,
        399.0926818847656,
        552.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "failures in the sublingual or intravenous groups, compared with 8 (53%) and 9 (81.8%)",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        552.03515625,
        399.0528869628906,
        565.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "in the oral and water groups respectively (p < 0.05). The approximate bioavailability",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        565.03515625,
        399.0827331542969,
        578.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "was 84% for sublingual administration. The mean (SD) time to reach a blood glucose",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        578.03515625,
        399.0529479980469,
        591.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "> 5.6 was 28.5 (10.6) minutes and 25.7 (9.5) for the sublingual and intravenous groups,",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        591.03515625,
        108.452880859375,
        604.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "respectively.",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        68.03150177001953,
        604.03515625,
        399.111572265625,
        617.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "Graz et al (2008) was an open-RCT of intravenous versus sublingual sugar in",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        56.692901611328125,
        617.03515625,
        399.102783203125,
        630.525146484375
      ],
      "text": "children with severe malaria and hypoglycaemia in Mali. Children were eligible if",
      "font": "MinionPro-Regular",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        223.39480590820312,
        644.9403076171875,
        231.64781188964844,
        655.2992553710938
      ],
      "text": "77",
      "font": "Helvetica-Condensed-Ligh",
      "size": 9.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}